# Exemptions for bin/check-provenance.  One per line:
#
#     <token>  <category>  <reason>
#
# CATEGORIES, and there are only two:
#
#   specimen — the token is quoted BECAUSE it is bad. Documentation of a
#              provenance fault has to name the fault. A `specimen` entry
#              asserts the value is false, so it cannot be used to launder a
#              fabricated pointer into passing: to exempt it you must declare it
#              wrong, which is the opposite of claiming it.
#
#   pruned   — the token was a real cohort whose roots have since been
#              garbage-collected. The pointer was honest when written and is now
#              unverifiable locally.
#
# EXEMPTIONS STAY CONVICTABLE. If a token listed here starts resolving, the
# entry is stale and the check says so — an allowlist that only ever grows is
# how a gate turns into decoration.

